  "question": {
    "text": "The line <math><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>12</mn></math> meets the coordinates axes at <math><mi>A</mi></math> and <math><mi>B</mi></math> respectively. The line through <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>5,5</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> perpendicular to <math><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi></math> meets the coordinate axes and the line <math><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi></math> at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>C</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>D</mi></math> and <math><mi>E</mi></math> respectively. If <math><mi>O</mi></math> is the origin, then the area (in sq. units) of the figure <math><mi>O</mi><mi>C</mi><mi>E</mi><mi>B</mi></math> is equal to<br />\r<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/nta_abhyas/jee_main/images/ed52a104-677c-4cac-8a01-29c6a8135e74.png\" style=\"width: 230px; height: 180px;\" />",
